The '''Macaio–Uxiu high speed rail line''', alternatively known as the '''Baixas''', is a {{convert|409.58|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 8 May 2003. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it connects the cities of [[Macaio]], [[Calatayud]] and [[Uxiu]] in 1 hour and 15 minutes. In Uxiu the line merges into the ''[[Transmatarrañya high speed rail line|Transmatarrañya]]'', which crosses the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]] towards [[Guadalajara]] to link the west and east coasts of [[Atlántida]].

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service. 

